He joins countless others in fending off

766
00:41:05,201 --> 00:41:07,620
the odorous molecules that invade our lives.

767
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:14,740
But in fighting stink so relentlessly,

768
00:41:14,741 --> 00:41:17,200
we're potentially creating more of an odor obsession

769
00:41:17,201 --> 00:41:19,200
for ourselves.

770
00:41:19,201 --> 00:41:21,580
The more that we, as a society,

771
00:41:21,581 --> 00:41:25,780
deal with reducing stinks, the more that stinks bug us.

772
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:29,080
Because you get rid of them, then when they are present,

773
00:41:29,180 --> 00:41:33,020
it's almost that much more offensive or strange or unusual.

774
00:41:33,120 --> 00:41:36,160
As populations grow and we generate more waste

775
00:41:36,260 --> 00:41:39,140
and raise more livestock, is life around us

776
00:41:39,240 --> 00:41:41,460
really getting stinkier?

777
00:41:41,560 --> 00:41:43,260
Or is it actually that we Americans

778
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:47,040
have gotten used to an overly stink-free existence?

779
00:41:47,140 --> 00:41:51,140
Either way, it's a testament to the power of stink.

780
00:41:51,580 --> 00:41:53,580
If you're going to test your breath at home,

781
00:41:53,581 --> 00:41:56,580
if you don't have a $3,000 limiter at home,

782
00:41:56,581 --> 00:41:59,580
the way you test your breath is lick the back of your hand.

783
00:41:59,581 --> 00:42:01,580
Make sure you lick your own hand when you do that, by the way.

784
00:42:01,581 --> 00:42:03,580
Let that dry a few seconds.

785
00:42:03,581 --> 00:42:04,580
And then smell that.

786
00:42:04,581 --> 00:42:08,580
If you do have bad breath, the sulfur compounds will stick to your hand

787
00:42:08,581 --> 00:42:11,580
once the liquid evaporates, and then you can smell it that way.

788
00:42:11,581 --> 00:42:13,580
I smell good, by the way.

